1.0.3 2026-10-30

  - Recorded data changed: the 226 BrainVision recordings (.eeg) whose three channels had different lengths, and
    which were NaN-padded at the end, are cropped to their shortest channel. Each new .eeg is a byte prefix of the
    old one (kept samples bit-identical, checked for all 226). Left out: up to 2256 time points per file (257,384
    in all); counted per channel, 360,481 real samples of the longer channels (at most 3,760 per file), which
    remain in the release .mat files in sourcedata/. Per-file old/new lengths, old annex key and new SHA-256:
    code/fix-20261030_crop_manifest.tsv.
  - Sidecars: RecordingDuration and RecordingDescription of the 226 ieeg.json, n_samples in the 14 scans.tsv and
    the scans.json description give the cropped lengths (code/fix-20261030_crop_text.py).
  - code/: crop and text scripts (fix-20261030_crop406.py, fix-20261030_crop_text.py), S3 fetch helper, the NaN
    scans of the uncropped files and the crop manifest.
  - README: the published text is kept unchanged; a paragraph and a section "Cropped recordings" added after it
    describe the crop.

1.0.2 2026-10-16
  - Restore the descriptive Name from v1.0.0 after the v1.0.1 naming regression.
1.0.0 2026-10-08
  - Initial iEEG-BIDS packaging of Zenodo record 7352058 (no signal processing).
